The function selects only the public columns from each row, so the docstring should say that, and note that objector contact details and internal notes are excluded. [tool_use propose_change {"path":"register/export.py","summary":"Add a docstring to export_comments describing its input, output, and the public-only column filtering.","diff":"--- a/register/export.py\n+++ b/register/export.py\n@@ -3,6 +3,15 @@\n PUBLIC_COLUMNS = ['reference', 'address', 'comment_date', 'stance', 'comment_text']\n \n def export_comments(rows):\n+    \"\"\"Return public-facing copies of comment rows.\n+\n+    Each row is reduced to the columns in PUBLIC_COLUMNS, so objector name,\n+    email, phone and internal_note are never included in the output.\n+\n+    Args:\n+        rows: iterable of mappings, each containing at least the PUBLIC_COLUMNS keys.\n+\n+    Returns:\n+        A list of dicts, one per input row, with only the public columns.\n+    \"\"\"\n     out = []\n     for row in rows:\n         out.append({c: row[c] for c in PUBLIC_COLUMNS})\n"}]
